@startuml CryptoWeb-state-01-conditional-order
title CryptoWeb - Conditional Order Lifecycle

!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 65
skinparam ranksep 65
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam StateFontSize 14
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
hide empty description

state "PENDING" as Pending
state "PROCESSING" as Processing
state "EXECUTED" as Executed
state "FAILED" as Failed
state "CANCELLED" as Cancelled

[*] --> Pending : valid order created
Pending --> Pending : edit price or quantity
Pending --> Processing : market trigger reached / atomic claim
Pending --> Cancelled : user cancels
Pending --> Cancelled : linked OCO order executes

Processing --> Executed : settlement and trade sync succeed
Processing --> Failed : non-retryable business error
Processing --> Pending : transient failure or missing acknowledgement
Processing --> Pending : stale processing reset

note left of Pending
  Only PENDING orders are editable
  and user-cancellable. The executor
  checks for triggers periodically.
end note

note right of Processing
  Execution uses the current market
  price. The user-specified order
  price is a trigger, not a guaranteed
  execution price.
end note

note right of Executed
  The corresponding trade is recorded
  using the order reference. Immediate
  market trades do not require an order.
end note

@enduml
